---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<style is:inline>
  .demo-component-card .demo-area {
    min-height: 20rem !important;
  }
</style>

<p class='text-body-medium'>
  A tooltip opens in the browser's top layer, so it shows above modals and menus. It describes its target
  through <code>aria-describedby</code>: the element whose id is in <code>for</code> (in the tooltip's own
  document or shadow root), or else its parent element. Escape hides a visible tooltip without closing the
  dialog or menu around it. <code>placement</code> takes <code>top</code> (default), <code>bottom</code>,
  <code>start</code> or <code>end</code>, optionally with <code>-start</code> or <code>-end</code> alignment.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html'>

  <span class='tooltiwc-link' tabindex='1'>
     hover here
      <wc-tooltip open>Save the record</wc-tooltip>
    </span>
</DemoComponentCard>

<br/>

<DemoComponentCard lang='html'>
  <div style='position:relative;'>
    <wc-button id='tooltip-btn' variant='outlined'><wc-icon slot='icon' name='save'></wc-icon></wc-button>
    <wc-tooltip for='tooltip-btn' placement='bottom'>Relative tooltip using the for attribute</wc-tooltip>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p class='text-body-medium'>
  For rich content with actions, use <a href='/components/popover'><code>wc-popover</code></a>.
</p>
